Aim: To perform regression testing automatically using Maven and Azure DevOps.
Steps to perform
1. Open IntelliJ IDEA.
2. Create a Maven project named RegressionTestingDev.
3. Select Java JDK and enable Create Git Repository.
4. Open pom.xml.
5. Add the JUnit 4.13.2 dependency.
6. Reload the Maven project.
7. Inside src/test/java, create the package org.example.
8. Create a Java test class named MainTest.java.
9. Enter the JUnit test code from your manual.
10. Run MainTest in IntelliJ and verify that the test passes.
11. Create a private GitHub repository named RegressionTestingDev.
12. Open the terminal and execute:
git init
git add .
git commit -m "regression"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin YOUR_REPOSITORY_URL
git push -u origin main


13. Open Azure DevOps and create a project named RegressionTestingDev.
14. Go to Pipelines → New Pipeline.
15. Select GitHub and choose your repository.
16. Authorize GitHub access if requested.
17. Choose Maven as the pipeline type.
18. Replace the generated YAML content with the pipeline code given in your manual.
19. Click Save and Run.
20. Open the Test Results tab to check whether the JUnit tests passed.
